                                            * The look-up table scheme also applies to the configuration                    D:\PICs\ControlBoard\autofiles\usbdsc.c
                                            * descriptor. A USB device may have multiple configuration                      D:\PICs\ControlBoard\autofiles\usbdsc.c
                                            * descriptors, i.e. CFG01, CFG02, etc. To add a configuration                   D:\PICs\ControlBoard\autofiles\usbdsc.c
                                            * descriptor, user must implement a structure similar to CFG01.                 D:\PICs\ControlBoard\autofiles\usbdsc.c
                                            * The next step is to add the configuration descriptor name, i.e.               D:\PICs\ControlBoard\autofiles\usbdsc.c
                                            * cfg01, cfg02,.., to the look-up table USB_CD_Ptr. USB_CD_Ptr[0]               D:\PICs\ControlBoard\autofiles\usbdsc.c
                                            * is a dummy place holder since configuration 0 is the un-configured            D:\PICs\ControlBoard\autofiles\usbdsc.c
